    "directions": [
      "Pre-heat the oven to 350. Add pretzels into a good processor and process until crumbly. Add in the peanut butter and rice malt syrup and pulse until you can pinch the mixture with your fingers and it sticks together.",
      "Transfer to a 8×8 round tart or cake pan and press down the mixture evenly, then place it into the oven for 10 minutes",
      "In the meantime, melt down your chocolate in a double-boiler or in the microwave",
      "Add the tofu, melted chocolate, instant coffee, coconut sugar and vanilla extract into a high speed blender and blend until smooth",
      "Once the crust has come out, allow it to cool, then pour over the chocolate filling and allow it to chill for at least 1 hour (best overnight)!",
      "Optional: Spread a layer of coconut whip cream over the top and sprinkle with crushed pretzels and shaved chocolate."
    ],
